  "output": "I'll analyze the codebase for performance issues and provide actionable recommendations.\n\n## Performance Analysis Report\n\n### 1. **Memory Leaks** 🔴 Critical\n\n#### Issue: Unbounded growth in processed log tracking\n**Location:** `use-action-cards.ts`, `use-chat.ts`, `use-socket.ts`\n\nThe `processedIds` Set and `processedLogIds` Set grow indefinitely and never clear old entries.\n\n**Fix:**\n```typescript\n// use-action-cards.ts\nexport function useActionCards(snapshot: A0Snapshot | null): UseActionCardsReturn {\n  const [cards, setCards] = useState<ActionCard[]>([]);\n  const processedIds = useRef(new Set<string>());\n  \n  // Add cleanup to prevent unbounded growth\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Clear processed IDs older than 1 hour to prevent memory leak\n    const cleanup = () => {\n      const oneHourAgo = Date.now() / 1000 - 3600;\n      setCards(prev => {\n        const recent = prev.filter(c => c.timestamp > oneHourAgo);\n        // Rebuild processedIds from recent cards only\n        processedIds.current = new Set(recent.map(c => c.id));\n        return recent;\n      });\n    };\n    \n    const interval = setInterval(cleanup, 300000); // Every 5 minutes\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\n  }, []);\n  \n  // ... rest of hook\n}\n```\n\n#### Issue: Timer cleanup in `use-expo-stream.ts`\nMultiple `setTimeout` calls may not be properly cleaned up.\n\n**Fix:**\n```typescript\nexport function useExpoStream(snapshot: A0Snapshot | null, chefStatus: ChefStatus | null): ExpoState {\n  const [expo, setExpo] = useState<ExpoState>({ text: null, active: false });\n  const timerRef = useRef<NodeJS.Timeout>();\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Clear any existing timer\n    if (timerRef.current) clearTimeout(timerRef.current);\n    \n    if (!chefStatus) return;\n\n    if (chefStatus.active) {\n      setExpo({ text: chefStatus.text, active: true });\n    } else {\n      setExpo({ text: chefStatus.text, active: false });\n      timerRef.current = setTimeout(() => {\n        setExpo((prev) => prev.active ? prev : { text: null, active: false });\n      }, 3000);\n    }\n    \n    return () => {\n      if (timerRef.current) clearTimeout(timerRef.current);\n    };\n  }, [chefStatus]);\n  \n  // ... rest of hook\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Unnecessary Re-renders** 🟡 High Priority\n\n#### Issue: Missing useCallback wrappers\n**Location:** `use-action-cards.ts`\n\n`markRead` and `markAllRead` are recreated on every render.\n\n**Fix:**\n```typescript\nimport { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from \"react\";\n\nexport function useActionCards(snapshot: A0Snapshot | null): UseActionCardsReturn {\n  // ... existing code ...\n\n  const markRead = useCallback((id: string) => {\n    setCards(prev => prev.map(c => c.id === id ? { ...c, read: true } : c));\n  }, []);\n\n  const markAllRead = useCallback(() => {\n    setCards(prev => prev.map(c => ({ ...c, read: true })));\n  }, []);\n\n  return { cards, unreadCount, markRead, markAllRead };\n}\n```\n\n#### Issue: Redundant effect in `use-chat.ts`\n**Location:** `use-chat.ts` lines 22-25\n\nSeparate effect just to sync `contextIdRef` is unnecessary.\n\n**Fix:**\n```typescript\n// Remove this effect entirely:\n// useEffect(() => {\n//   contextIdRef.current = contextId;\n// }, [contextId]);\n\n// Instead, update contextIdRef wherever you update contextId state:\nconst newContextId = data.context || contextIdRef.current;\nif (newContextId) {\n  setContextId(newContextId);\n  contextIdRef.current = newContextId; // Update ref immediately\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Redundant Computations** 🟡 High Priority\n\n#### Issue: Repeated formatting in table rows\n**Location:** All workspace pages (orders, inventory, food-cost, etc.)\n\nFunctions like `formatCurrency`, `formatDate`, `parseNum` are called on every render for every row.\n\n**Fix using memoization:**\n```typescript\n// food-cost/page.tsx (and similar in other pages)\nconst processedItems = useMemo(() => {\n  return data.map(item => ({\n    ...item,\n    // Pre-compute formatted values once\n    displayCost: formatCurrency(item.current_cost_pct),\n    parsedCost: parseNum(item.current_cost_pct),\n    displayDate: formatDate(item.updated_at),\n    pressure: normalizePressure(item.pressure),\n  }));\n}, [data]);\n\n// Then use processedItems in your filter/render logic\nconst filtered = useMemo(() => {\n  let result = processedItems;\n  if (activeFilter !== \"All\") {\n    result = result.filter(item => item.pressure === activeFilter);\n  }\n  if (searchTerm) {\n    result = result.filter(item =>\n      item.menu_item_name.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase())\n    );\n  }\n  return result;\n}, [processedItems, activeFilter, searchTerm]);\n```\n\n#### Issue: URL construction on every render\n**Location:** `use-workspace.ts`\n\n**Fix:**\n```typescript\nexport function useWorkspace<T = Record<string, unknown>>(\n  endpoint: string,\n  locationId?: string,\n): UseWorkspaceReturn<T> {\n  const [data, setData] = useState<T[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [refreshKey, setRefreshKey] = useState(0);\n\n  // Memoize URL construction\n  const url = useMemo(() => {\n    return locationId ? `${endpoint}?location_id=${locationId}` : endpoint;\n  }, [endpoint, locationId]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    setLoading(true);\n    fetch(url, { credentials: \"include\" })\n      .then(async (res) => {\n        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`${res.status}`);\n        const json = await res.json();\n        setData(Array.isArray(json) ? json : json.items ?? json.data ?? []);\n        setError(null);\n      })\n      .catch((err) => {\n        setError(err.message);\n        setData([]);\n      })\n      .finally(() => setLoading(false));\n  }, [url, refreshKey]); // Use memoized URL\n\n  return { data, loading, error, refresh: () => setRefreshKey((k) => k + 1) };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Caching Opportunities** 🟢 Medium Priority\n\n#### Opportunity: Add SWR or React Query for data fetching\n**Location:** `use-workspace.ts`\n\nReplace manual fetch with SWR for automatic caching, revalidation, and deduplication.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```typescript\n// Install: pnpm add swr\n\nimport useSWR from 'swr';\n\nconst fetcher = (url: string) =>\n  fetch(url, { credentials: \"include\" }).then(async (res) => {\n    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`${res.status}`);\n    const json = await res.json();\n    return Array.isArray(json) ? json : json.items ?? json.data ?? [];\n  });\n\nexport function useWorkspace<T = Record<string, unknown>>(\n  endpoint: string,\n  locationId?: string,\n): UseWorkspaceReturn<T> {\n  const url = locationId ? `${endpoint}?location_id=${locationId}` : endpoint;\n  \n  const { data, error, isLoading, mutate } = useSWR<T[]>(url, fetcher, {\n    revalidateOnFocus: false,\n    dedupingInterval: 10000, // Dedupe requests within 10s\n  });\n\n  return {\n    data: data ?? [],\n    loading: isLoading,\n    error: error?.message ?? null,\n    refresh: mutate,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Automatic caching across page navigations\n- Request deduplication\n- Stale-while-revalidate pattern\n- Focus revalidation\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Virtual Scrolling for Large Lists** 🟢 Medium Priority\n\n#### Issue: Large tables render all rows at once\n**Location:** All workspace pages with tables\n\nFor tables with 100+ rows, implement virtual scrolling.\n\n**Implementation:**\n```typescript\n// Install: pnpm add @tanstack/react-virtual\n\nimport { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';\n\n// Example for orders page\nfunction OrdersTable({ orders }: { orders: Order[] }) {\n  const parentRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  \n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: orders.length,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: () => 60, // Estimated row height\n    overscan: 5,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div ref={parentRef} className=\"h-[600px] overflow-auto\">\n      <Table>\n        <TableHeader>\n          {/* ... headers ... */}\n        </TableHeader>\n        <TableBody style={{ height: `${virtualizer.getTotalSize()}px` }}>\n          {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualRow) => {\n            const order = orders[virtualRow.index];\n            return (\n              <TableRow\n                key={order.id}\n                style={{\n                  position: 'absolute',\n                  top: 0,\n                  left: 0,\n                  width: '100%',\n                  transform: `translateY(${virtualRow.start}px)`,\n                }}\n              >\n                {/* ... cells ... */}\n              </TableRow>\n            );\n          })}\n        </TableBody>\n      </Table>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Optimize Framer Motion** 🟢 Medium Priority\n\n#### Issue: Too many animated elements\nAnimating every table row causes performance issues with large datasets.\n\n**Fix:**\n```typescript\n// Only animate first 20 rows, instant render rest\n<AnimatePresence mode=\"popLayout\">\n  {filtered.slice(0, 20).map((order, i) => (\n    <motion.tr\n      key={order.id}\n      custom={i}\n      variants={rowVariants}\n      initial=\"hidden\"\n      animate=\"visible\"\n    >\n      {/* ... */}\n    </motion.tr>\n  ))}\n  {filtered.slice(20).map((order) => (\n    <tr key={order.id}>\n      {/* No animation for rows beyond 20 */}\n    </tr>\n  ))}\n</AnimatePresence>\n```\n\nOr use `layout` prop instead of full animations:\n```typescript\n<motion.tr layout transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}>\n  {/* Cheaper layout animations */}\n</motion.tr>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Impact\n\n| Issue | Severity | Impact | Effort |\n|-------|----------|--------|--------|\n| Unbounded Set growth (memory leak) | 🔴 Critical | High | Low |\n| Missing useCallback | 🟡 High | Medium | Low |\n| Repeated formatting | 🟡 High | Medium | Medium |\n| No data caching (SWR) | 🟢 Medium | High | Medium |\n| Virtual scrolling | 🟢 Medium | High | High |\n| Excessive animations | 🟢 Medium | Medium | Low |\n\n**Quick wins (implement first):**\n1. Fix memory leaks in processed IDs (30 min)\n2. Add useCallback wrappers (15 min)\n3. Memoize formatted values (1 hour)\n4. Limit animated rows (30 min)\n\n**High-value investments:**\n1. Implement SWR for caching (2-3 hours)\n2. Add virtual scrolling to workspace tables (4-6 hours)\n",
